al.","They need not be the same sequence, because order matters."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ba26ba348e75e4d9e3731ac9"},{"id":"sequence_new_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In the notation $(a_n)_{n\\ge m}$, what does the index $n$ do?","options":["It gives the value of every term.","It labels each term's position in the order.","It makes the collection unordered.","It forces the sequence to be finite."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9a68395ec73e4f4fa1e970d0"},{"id":"sequence_new_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $a_1=1$ and $a_{n+1}=a_n+2$, what is $a_4$?","options":["$7$","$8$","$6$","$9$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"95e0738419c66215d28c3618"},{"id":"sequence_new_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"How many distinct values appear in the range of the sequence $1,1,1,\\ldots$?","options":["$1$","infinitely many","$3$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"46afef1e412a54ab7d5d414d"},{"id":"sequence_new_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For the sequence $a_n=n^2$ with $n\\ge1$, what is $a_3$?","options":["$9$","$6$","$3$","$8$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fda9e0c2d8ed4d64667a3893"},{"id":"sequence_new_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $a_n=(-1)^n$ with $n\\ge1$, what are the first three terms?","options":["$1,-1,1$","$0,1,0$","$-1,-1,-1$","$-1,1,-1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9e8f80d9b6db3754a18e448f"},{"id":"sequence_new_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which object is a finite sequence?","options":["$\\{a_1,a_2,a_3\\}$ as an unordered set only","$a/b$","$(a_1,a_2,a_3)$","$\\sup E$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3ef3cee3d8ac16cadc1eabf9"},{"id":"sequence_new_019","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does it mean to view a sequence as a function?","options":["Each term must be an integer.","Each integer index is assigned exactly one term.","The sequence must be unordered.","The sequence must have a maximum term."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"273793887dc390512fbec67f"},{"id":"sequence_new_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What distinguishes a finite sequence from an infinite one?","options":["Its index set is finite","It has no order","Its terms must repeat","It cannot contain numbers"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9aa39b640990195ec19454c5"}]}}